# Line endings are LF, in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# This repo had nine CRLF files against twenty LF ones, with nothing recording
# which was intended. Any editor or script that normalised on write turned a
# one-line change into a whole-file diff.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text and store it with LF; `eol=lf` checks it back
# out with LF everywhere, including Windows, so the working tree agrees with the
# repository. Binary content is detected automatically and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
